    },
    {
      "item": "Concentration Risk Controls and measures to minimize undue concentration of exposure in the Group’s two client segments. These include portfolio and counter- party limits, as well as approval and review controls. The concentration risk per name and group concentration, economic sec- tor, and business segment was closely monitored, and efforts were deployed to minimize the concentration risk to the maximum allowable limits. Notable efforts were made by the Bank of Kigali to maintain a more strategically diverse portfolio by promoting lending services to retail and SME clients.",
